course: dictionary
lesson: 5366
title: Kitchen: a room or a team
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. Kitchen is one of those words. Its first meaning is a room where food is stored, prepared and cooked. Its second meaning is the people who cook in a restaurant.
explain: «The kitchen is busy tonight, with orders coming in fast.» Are the orders going into a room? No. Orders come in to the people who cook, so here kitchen means the cooks. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
explain: «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» The clues are knives, hot pans and slippery floors. They show that the kitchen is a place that needs care, so the word means the room.
explain: Kitchen also appears in phrases such as «kitchen table», «kitchen sink» and «kitchen knife». In each one, the word tells you where the thing is or what it is for. When you meet a phrase you do not know, read the words around it.
fact: Kitchen is a noun: a kitchen, kitchens.
fact: Meaning 1: the room where food is stored, prepared and cooked.
fact: Meaning 2: the people who cook in a restaurant.
fact: Kitchen safety: turn pan handles in, never leave cooking alone, and let an adult help with heat and knives.
fact: Phrases with kitchen: kitchen table, kitchen sink, kitchen knife, kitchen roll and kitchen garden.
exercise: «The kitchen is busy tonight, with orders coming in fast.» What does kitchen mean here? | *The cooks who prepare the food in the restaurant | A room for sleeping | A bus stop | The front door
exercise: «Walk, never run, in the kitchen.» Why should you not run in the kitchen? | Running makes the floor warmer | *Knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous | The kitchen floor is made of glass | Running is rude to the cook
exercise: Which is a kitchen safety rule? | Run across the floor carrying a sharp knife | Put hot pans on the floor to cool | *Turn pan handles in, so they cannot be knocked | Leave the hob on and go out of the room
test: «A family left a pan of oil on the hob and went to answer the door.» What is the danger? | *The hot oil could catch fire | The oil will turn into a cake | The oil will make a loud noise only | The door is too heavy to open
test: «Some surprises hide in the kitchen: a potato is a swollen stem, not a root.» Which statement matches this? | A potato is a root, like a carrot | A kitchen is a type of bus | *A potato is a swollen stem, not a root | A banana is a shoe
exam: Which sentence uses kitchen to mean the room? | The kitchen said the soup was ready | *Wash your hands before you start cooking in the kitchen | The kitchen is busy with orders tonight | The kitchen made a loud complaint to the manager
